WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.201
This just in to CNN.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.202
We have an update on

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.436
Mitch McConnell's health.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:03.937
Coming in,

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.106
the Senate Republican leader's office

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.208
has just released some new details.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:08.942
I want to bring in CNN's

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.410
Manu Raju and CNN chief

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.812
medical correspondent, Dr. Sanjay Gupta.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.981
You've got your hands on this release.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.182
What does it say?

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.450
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.518
Giving more details

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.452
after the second

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:20.487
health scare involving

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.322
Senate Republican Leader Mitch McConnell,

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.391
who, as we remember, froze last week

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.291
in front of cameras

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.259
for roughly 30 seconds.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.294
That also occurred back in July.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.263
And this also in the aftermath of him

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.132
hitting his head, suffering a concussion

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:32.932
back in March,

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.701
this providing more information

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.802
in the aftermath of that

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.003
second health scare.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:37.971
So this is a letter

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.572
that was released by McConnell's office

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.641
from Brian Monahan, who is a Capitol Hill

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.443
attending physician as a brief letter.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.511
So I will read it to you

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.045
in full

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.780
says My examination of you

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.049
following your August 30th 2023

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.016
brief episode

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:52.218
includes several medical evaluations.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.288
It says brain MRI imaging, EEG study

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.556
and consultations

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.891
with several neurologists

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.093
for a comprehensive neurology assessment.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.294
And it goes on to say,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.862
there is no evidence

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.631
that you have a seizure disorder

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.332
or that you experience a stroke.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.068
Tia, or movement disorders

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.070
such as Parkinson's disease.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.072
There are no changes recommended

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.473
in treatment protocols

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.075
as you continue recovery

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.577
from your March 2023 fall.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.711
So there's

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.180
been a

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.114
lot of questions about

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.415
what exactly happened

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.283
to Senator McConnell.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.384
Republicans are coming back

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.585
and the Senate and Democrats

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.719
coming back to the Senate

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.488
for the first time in roughly

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:30.390
five weeks on a recess.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.192
And the Republican leader

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.460
facing questions himself

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.994
about how long he can continue

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.129
to serve in office.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.430
Now, for the first time,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.432
providing information about that,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.134
he had these examinations

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.569
that there is no evidence of a seizure

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.236
or a stroke.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.170
A lot of speculation

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.505
that that could have been the case

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.306
at the time, John.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.007
As you know, Republicans.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.309
The leader's office

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.176
only indicated

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.911
that he had lightheadedness as well.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:52.712
They attributed

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.414
those two frozen moments to

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.181
and that's

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.283
last week when Brian Monahan, the Capitol

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.418
physician, released a letter.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.520
He said lightheadedness could occur

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.354
from those

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.122
who suffered

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.389
a concussion, as McConnell

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.592
did back in March.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.493
So it's

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.560
it was unclear exactly

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.063
whether it was tied to that fall or not.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:10.763
But here

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.298
indicating in this note,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.033
they say no evidence of a seizure

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:14.734
or a stroke.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.536
The question is, are Parkinson's disease?

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.337
The question is,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.305
will that alleviate any concerns

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.141
that are lingering on Capitol Hill?

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.275
Monti, thank you for jumping on

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.744
so quickly to bring us this update.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:27.480
Sanjay, not only as a

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:28.748
as a dear friend and chief

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.616
medical correspondent,

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:32.051
but neuro neurosurgeon in your own right.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:32.886
Talk to me

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:33.353
about what

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:33.887
you hear

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.621
from the Capitol

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.891
physician here that they did MRI imaging

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.893
and EEG study

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.927
and other consultations

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.295
with several neurologists.

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:44.898
Well, it sounds

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:45.098
like they

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.833
did a pretty comprehensive

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.967
sort of evaluation.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:48.801
So this was,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.670
I think, a man who said August 30th,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.305
so a few days ago now.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.373
So apparently

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.440
after that last episode,

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.143
it sounds like there was enough concern.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.144
It doesn't sound like they did

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.512
these types of tests in

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.681
July after that first episode.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.250
But after this most recent episode,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.486
you know, the idea that was this a stroke

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.021
or was this a seizure

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.455
or was this something else

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.490
like a movement?

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.091
Disorders such as Parkinson's

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.327
and medications not wearing

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.828
not working well.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.863
It sounds like they evaluated

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:20.133
for all those things, brain MRI, EEG

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.403
and then neurological evaluation

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.003
sounds like

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.306
and basically saying none of those things

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.608
seem to be the case here.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.143
So that's that's good.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.144
That's good news.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.012
I think I'm curious to know

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.147
what kind of follow up.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:34.380
You know,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.082
when you do these types of imaging tests

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.217
or do an EEG,

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.518
you're getting sort of these

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.954
these snapshots in time.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.555
So sometimes things may be happening,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.923
but you don't catch them on the scans.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:44.791
But nevertheless, it's

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.626
a pretty thorough evaluation.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.361
And as Manu said,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.495
they're basically saying, look,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.431
he had this concussion back earlier

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.198
in the spring.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.101
As a result of that

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.002
lightheadedness,

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.604
which is a little bit of a tough line

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.071
to draw

00:03:58.071 --> 00:03:59.272
between the concussions,

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.274
lightheadedness and these symptoms.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.543
But that's basically

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.344
what this note is saying.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.346
We've ruled out

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:06.913
some of the

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.215
the leading other possible things here.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.318
That's what the note specifically does

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.320
it says what it's not.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.289
It says no evidence of seizure,

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.223
no evidence of stroke,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.392
no evidence of TIA, no Parkinson's.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.961
It does not do as much to, say,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.631
definitive of fully what it is.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:25.965
There's a suggestion

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.233
it is connected to the concussion.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.102
Sanjay, in your field.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.137
And again, this is very much your field.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.274
Can you always know what it is or can

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.876
all you do is to rule things out

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.413
Yeah, that's a great question.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.147
Sometimes you'll get

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.782
a definitive diagnosis.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:43.850
I mean, something pops out.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:44.851
You do an EEG

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.918
and someone is clearly

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.954
having a certain type of seizure

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.155
which could explain those symptoms

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.758
that would rule in the diagnosis.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.059
But yeah, a lot of times

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.093
with something like this,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.428
you are saying, hey, look,

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:56.729
what are the worst things

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:57.997
that could possibly be causing this?

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:58.665
You want to

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.199
you want to hope for the best,

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.534
but prepare for the worst.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.336
That sort of mentality.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.471
So you look at the worst possible things

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.106
and start to rule them out.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.775
A brain MRI

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:10.510
is there blood, blood collection

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.044
still in the brain?

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:11.811
Is there a tumor

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.613
or is there something else there?

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.315
It sounds like the brain MRI.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:16.416
They don't say that definitively,

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:17.417
but they say

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.885
basically give you the impression

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:21.521
that it was normal, an EEG,

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.489
no evidence of a seizure disorder.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.425
So those are those are pretty good tests.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.059
And then it sounds like

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:27.093
he had neurologists

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:27.960
also evaluate

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.962
him do a full exam to see

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.064
does he have any evidence

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:32.598
of Parkinson's disease,

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.933
a movement disorder,

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:34.667
which oftentimes

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:35.702
you can diagnose by

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.937
doing a good neurological exam.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.605
So they've looked at sort of the the

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.874
the the worst things, frankly,

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:42.575
that could be causing

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.676
these types of symptoms,

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.211
these freezing episodes,

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.312
and basically saying

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.380
we don't find anything

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.214
here at this point.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:48.948
So it's good news.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.049
I mean, it's it's

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.051
good for him to know that

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:52.518
what I think

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.953
is still confusing a bit,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.287
John,

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.022
I guess to your point, is concussion

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.957
in the spring lightheadedness.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:59.359
Yeah, that could be one of the symptoms.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.159
It's not something you put

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.561
at the top of the list.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:01.994
And certainly

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.763
you would just hydrate for that.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.131
If this is a problem,

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.466
why not just make sure

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:07.567
